<section class="section section-sm" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="label reveal">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-h2 reveal reveal-delay-1" id="faq-heading">Common questions</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item reveal">
        <summary>Do I need to know how to code?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>No. If you can have a conversation with Claude, you can use Quillby.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <summary>Does it work for any niche?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Tech, law, finance, health, education, marketing — any field with content online.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <summary>I have multiple clients. Will they mix?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>No. Each workspace has its own memory and sources. Client A never bleeds into Client B.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <summary>Is my data safe?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Everything runs on your machine. Nothing leaves it. The code is open source and auditable.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Is it free?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Local mode is completely free. Always will be. A Cloud mode with shared workspaces and a team dashboard is in development.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Do I need Claude Desktop?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Quillby connects to Claude Desktop with one click. It gives Claude new abilities — scanning feeds, drafting posts, planning campaigns — without leaving the chat.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Does it learn my writing style?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Every draft you save becomes a voice example. Over time Quillby adapts to your tone, vocabulary, and sentence rhythm. Different workspaces can have different voices.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Can I plan content ahead of time?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Quillby has a campaign system for multi-stage content series, a task board to track progress, and a calendar to see what's publishing when. All inside Claude.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Can it generate images or audio?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Quillby can generate images and audio if you connect a supported service like OpenAI or ElevenLabs. This is an optional add-on — the core brief-to-draft workflow works with nothing else to configure.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal reveal-delay-4">
        <summary>Is Quillby open source?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. MIT licensed. The full source is on <a href="https://github.com/vncsleal/quillby" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="faq-link">GitHub</a>. You can inspect it, fork it, or contribute.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(el => {
    const details = el as HTMLDetailsElement;
    const summary = details.querySelector('summary');
    if (!summary) return;

    summary.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      if (details.open) {
        details.classList.add('is-closing');
        const body = details.querySelector('.faq-body') as HTMLElement;
        body.addEventListener('transitionend', () => {
          details.open = false;
          details.classList.remove('is-closing');
        }, { once: true });
      } else {
        details.open = true;
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .faq-list {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .faq-list .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .faq-item > summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .faq-item > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .faq-item > summary:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .faq-item > summary::after {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--faint);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    line-height: 1;
    transition: transform 0.35s var(--ease-out), color 0.2s;
  }

  .faq-item[open] > summary::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .faq-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows 0.4s var(--ease-out);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-body,
  .faq-item.is-opening .faq-body {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  .faq-item.is-closing .faq-body {
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
  }

  .faq-body > p {
    min-height: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-bottom: 1.375rem;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .faq-link {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: opacity 0.15s;
  }

  .faq-link:hover { opacity: 0.7; }
</style>
